1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:18,373 --> 00:00:21,626
14 YEARS AGO

3
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:26,798
Hello.

4
00:00:26,881 --> 00:00:29,008
I'm Hong Man-su's legal guardian.

5
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:32,762
About the caregiver fees…

6
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:37,267
I know I'm really behind on payments,
but could I pay part of it now--

7
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:40,812
Mr. Hong Man-su hasn't had
a caregiver for a while.

8
00:00:40,895 --> 00:00:41,771
Sorry?

9
00:00:42,522 --> 00:00:45,900
I've been so busy with life
that I haven't been able to visit.

10
00:00:46,401 --> 00:00:50,363
Then how has a stroke patient
who can't use his limbs been getting by…

11
00:00:50,446 --> 00:00:53,700
Your son has been coming daily
to take care of him. Didn't you know?

12
00:00:53,783 --> 00:00:54,951
My son?

13
00:01:00,582 --> 00:01:02,500
Bet you're feeling nice and clean now.

14
00:01:14,429 --> 00:01:16,097
That darn punk.

15
00:01:22,228 --> 00:01:26,608
Why are you wasting your energy here
when you'll soon be training at Taereung?

16
00:01:27,942 --> 00:01:31,154
I have plenty of energy to spare
because you made me train so hard.

17
00:01:31,988 --> 00:01:34,866
This isn't why I made you train.
I made you train to box.

18
00:01:34,949 --> 00:01:37,368
I don't need to train to become the best.

19
00:01:39,704 --> 00:01:42,498
Stop looking into stuff like this,

20
00:01:43,041 --> 00:01:43,875
okay?

21
00:01:43,958 --> 00:01:46,377
Who'd be mad enough to hand out
30 million won?

22
00:01:46,461 --> 00:01:48,129
They're just after your organs.

23
00:01:49,172 --> 00:01:50,298
Goodness.

24
00:01:52,508 --> 00:01:53,509
Good grief.

25
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:55,011
Son, my foot.

26
00:01:55,094 --> 00:01:57,513
How does this punk look anything like me?

27
00:01:58,431 --> 00:02:00,558
If anyone should be offended, it's me.

28
00:02:01,059 --> 00:02:02,477
We look nothing alike.

29
00:02:03,144 --> 00:02:03,978
Hey.

30
00:02:04,479 --> 00:02:08,149
Life's been rough on me,
but I looked sharp back in the day.

31
00:02:13,905 --> 00:02:15,949
And I'm still a bachelor!

32
00:02:16,741 --> 00:02:20,286
How the heck…
do we look like father and son?

33
00:02:20,787 --> 00:02:22,080
Father and son, my ass.

34
00:02:30,004 --> 00:02:31,256
What are you laughing at?

35
00:02:41,266 --> 00:02:42,517
What are you looking at?

36
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:02,370
Jeong-hwa said she'd just stop by
Song-wol's for a bit.

37
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:04,580
Why isn't she back yet?

38
00:03:27,145 --> 00:03:28,396
Who are you?

39
00:03:28,896 --> 00:03:30,356
Who the hell are you?

40
00:03:33,109 --> 00:03:35,945
Jeong-hwa!

41
00:03:36,029 --> 00:03:36,904
You bastards!

42
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,615
Bastards! Jeong-hwa!

43
00:03:40,199 --> 00:03:41,200
Jeong-hwa!

44
00:03:45,538 --> 00:03:46,497
No!

45
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:49,000
Jeong-hwa!

46
00:03:50,877 --> 00:03:54,047
No!

47
00:03:55,882 --> 00:03:57,842
Let go!

48
00:03:59,844 --> 00:04:01,512
Jeong-hwa!

49
00:04:02,096 --> 00:04:04,182
Jeong-hwa!

50
00:04:04,682 --> 00:04:07,268
Damn it! Jeong-hwa!

51
00:04:07,769 --> 00:04:09,187
What do I do?

52
00:04:18,654 --> 00:04:19,781
My Jeong-hwa.

53
00:04:45,098 --> 00:04:45,973
Excuse me.

54
00:04:47,016 --> 00:04:48,184
How did it go?

55
00:04:48,267 --> 00:04:49,560
Did she make it?

56
00:04:50,186 --> 00:04:51,938
-The surgery went well, but…
-Yes?

57
00:04:52,021 --> 00:04:56,567
She lost a lot of blood,
so it's hard to say if she'll recover.

58
00:04:58,152 --> 00:05:00,029
-So…
-Yes.

59
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:01,781
Tonight will be critical.

60
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:05,326
We can only hope that she will hold on.

61
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:09,205
-Doctor.
-Sir, please. Calm down.

62
00:05:09,288 --> 00:05:12,708
We did our best,
so let's hold onto hope and wait.

63
00:05:22,969 --> 00:05:24,053
Jeong-hwa.

64
00:05:29,934 --> 00:05:30,768
Coach.

65
00:05:45,992 --> 00:05:47,452
Let's talk later.

66
00:07:18,668 --> 00:07:20,086
I know what you're planning.

67
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,005
Go on and try.

68
00:07:23,089 --> 00:07:26,384
But every day,
your imagination will eat away at you,

69
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:31,847
wondering… about my plan for you.

70
00:08:56,557 --> 00:08:58,225
Get the bastard!

71
00:09:47,858 --> 00:09:49,235
Let's end this now.

72
00:09:56,992 --> 00:09:58,619
This, the world's best wine…

73
00:09:59,537 --> 00:10:03,124
I hear the two families
who made it together for over 60 years

74
00:10:04,709 --> 00:10:07,545
eventually turned on each other
and went their separate ways.

75
00:10:13,217 --> 00:10:16,011
Even the greatest friendships
can't last forever.

76
00:10:21,767 --> 00:10:24,603
Even if it's Hong Do-yeop and Jang Tae-ha.

77
00:10:28,357 --> 00:10:29,191
Drink.

78
00:10:31,193 --> 00:10:32,236
I'll wait

79
00:10:33,946 --> 00:10:35,531
for you to finish that last glass.

80
00:12:08,749 --> 00:12:10,501
Why are you going this far?

81
00:12:11,544 --> 00:12:13,128
Scum like you…

82
00:12:15,047 --> 00:12:16,465
will never understand.

83
00:12:22,388 --> 00:12:25,724
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

84
00:12:25,808 --> 00:12:28,394
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

85
00:12:28,477 --> 00:12:30,813
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

86
00:12:32,898 --> 00:12:35,776
You haven't changed one bit,
Baek Sang-gil.

87
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:40,155
There's something in this world
that you can never win against.

88
00:12:42,157 --> 00:12:43,576
You lost.

89
00:13:11,937 --> 00:13:13,022
Baek Sang-gil!

90
00:13:18,068 --> 00:13:18,903
Baek…

91
00:13:48,557 --> 00:13:51,727
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

92
00:13:52,728 --> 00:13:56,690
Mr. Baek Sang-gil, you're under arrest for
bribery under Article 133, paragraph 1,

93
00:13:58,525 --> 00:14:00,611
and for attempted murder.

94
00:14:12,039 --> 00:14:12,873
You were hurt?

95
00:14:13,916 --> 00:14:16,418
While trying to catch Ju Min-jong
and Baek Sang-gil?

96
00:14:16,502 --> 00:14:17,419
Yes, sir.

97
00:14:17,503 --> 00:14:19,630
I lost my memory, so I couldn't come back.

98
00:14:19,713 --> 00:14:22,841
Your supervisor said
you applied for long-term sick leave.

99
00:14:24,635 --> 00:14:27,012
They must have people
in the prosecution office too.

100
00:14:27,763 --> 00:14:31,517
If we make a fuss, word could get out
about the emergency arrest.

101
00:14:32,101 --> 00:14:35,938
Please assign your most trustworthy
investigators and police officers to me.

102
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:43,028
Prosecutor.

103
00:14:43,529 --> 00:14:47,408
We've located and are ready to arrest
Baek Sang-gil and Ju Min-jong.

104
00:14:49,284 --> 00:14:50,160
Let's go.

105
00:14:51,161 --> 00:14:52,997
PROSECUTOR GO JI-WON

106
00:15:06,885 --> 00:15:10,264
You have the right to remain silent
and the right to an attorney,

107
00:15:10,347 --> 00:15:11,849
but we'll talk more

108
00:15:12,433 --> 00:15:14,852
at the prosecution office
as suspect and prosecutor.

109
00:15:29,033 --> 00:15:29,867
Jang Tae-ha.

110
00:15:32,703 --> 00:15:33,787
Are you okay?

111
00:15:36,373 --> 00:15:37,499
Why are you…

112
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,710
Why on earth are you here?

113
00:15:42,463 --> 00:15:43,297
Your memory…

114
00:15:44,923 --> 00:15:45,799
Yes.

115
00:15:47,176 --> 00:15:48,260
It's back.

116
00:15:51,722 --> 00:15:52,556
Okay.

117
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:54,099
You don't have to worry now.

118
00:15:55,434 --> 00:15:58,479
I caught him, so don't worry.

119
00:16:16,914 --> 00:16:20,793
Early this morning, Mirae Eden's
Chairman Baek and Mayor Ju of Gangju City

120
00:16:20,876 --> 00:16:23,462
were arrested on charges of bribery.

121
00:16:23,545 --> 00:16:26,882
The prosecution announced
they proceeded with the arrest

122
00:16:26,965 --> 00:16:30,135
after an internal investigation
uncovered clear evidence of bribery.

123
00:16:30,219 --> 00:16:32,888
At the time of Chairman Baek Sang-gil's
emergency arrest,

124
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:35,766
he was found threatening Mr. A,
a former Mirae Eden executive…

125
00:16:35,849 --> 00:16:37,184
Tae-ha?

126
00:16:37,267 --> 00:16:39,812
…and will also be investigated
for attempted murder.

127
00:16:40,479 --> 00:16:42,648
It is reported that Mr. A is currently

128
00:16:42,731 --> 00:16:45,984
in noncritical condition
and cooperating with the investigation.

129
00:17:10,843 --> 00:17:12,010
Are you okay?

130
00:17:16,890 --> 00:17:19,393
I got my memory back on the stowaway boat.

131
00:17:19,476 --> 00:17:22,729
Everyone must have thought
it was best for me to leave,

132
00:17:22,813 --> 00:17:24,731
but I had evidence to catch Baek Sang-gil.

133
00:17:24,815 --> 00:17:26,900
That's why I came back.

134
00:17:32,406 --> 00:17:34,491
Thank you for saving me

135
00:17:35,617 --> 00:17:39,288
and for keeping me safe all this time.

136
00:17:40,914 --> 00:17:42,624
I'll take care of things from now on.

137
00:17:42,708 --> 00:17:45,043
I'll gather evidence,
including for Jeong-hwa,

138
00:17:45,127 --> 00:17:48,463
and make sure Baek Sang-gil gets
the maximum possible sentence.

139
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:57,514
Yes?

140
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:01,727
Prosecutor, the chief is looking for you.

141
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:02,644
Okay.

142
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:08,483
Take good care of yourself.

143
00:18:36,553 --> 00:18:39,890
Please summon Baek Sang-gil to
the prosecutor's office for questioning.

144
00:18:39,973 --> 00:18:41,016
Understood.

145
00:19:04,873 --> 00:19:06,041
Jang Tae-ha.

146
00:19:20,013 --> 00:19:21,306
You crazy bastard.

147
00:19:25,852 --> 00:19:28,397
You risked your life
to catch that despicable dog?

148
00:19:30,732 --> 00:19:32,943
Don't you know what your life is worth?

149
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:37,489
Your grandma cherished you beyond measure
and raised you so preciously.

150
00:19:37,572 --> 00:19:41,618
And at one point,
you were the pride of the whole village!

151
00:19:42,911 --> 00:19:43,829
And to me…

152
00:19:45,747 --> 00:19:46,873
To me…

153
00:19:51,628 --> 00:19:54,381
you're like a thorn
lodged deep in my heart.

154
00:20:18,739 --> 00:20:19,823
You're awake?

155
00:20:21,908 --> 00:20:23,201
Can you hear me?

156
00:20:26,246 --> 00:20:29,291
I can take a beating, can't I?

157
00:20:33,837 --> 00:20:35,589
I was so scared.

158
00:20:39,843 --> 00:20:41,261
Don't cry.

159
00:20:42,346 --> 00:20:43,847
Thank you for staying with me.

160
00:20:45,265 --> 00:20:46,933
Thank you for waking up.

161
00:20:47,559 --> 00:20:50,020
Thank you, honey.

162
00:21:07,412 --> 00:21:09,956
How's Tae-ha doing?

163
00:21:15,837 --> 00:21:19,424
Let's talk about that later
when you're all better.

164
00:21:22,469 --> 00:21:24,805
You said that the day
Tae-ha quit the national team,

165
00:21:25,305 --> 00:21:26,515
you

166
00:21:27,682 --> 00:21:30,852
cried like an animal
that failed to protect its cub.

167
00:21:50,455 --> 00:21:51,957
You felt so bad about that,

168
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:55,836
which is why you came to Taffy Village
to watch over Tae-ha's grandma.

169
00:21:58,004 --> 00:22:00,340
Which is where you met pretty old me.

170
00:22:04,010 --> 00:22:07,848
So hurry and go see Tae-ha.

171
00:22:12,269 --> 00:22:15,689
I'm sure Tae-ha's heart is bruised,

172
00:22:16,773 --> 00:22:18,400
but there's also

173
00:22:18,984 --> 00:22:20,694
a thorn stuck deep in your heart.

174
00:22:22,821 --> 00:22:26,074
Use this to pull out that thorn.

175
00:22:27,784 --> 00:22:28,618
Okay?

176
00:22:37,752 --> 00:22:42,507
If you risk your precious life again
because of a bastard who's barely human,

177
00:22:43,008 --> 00:22:45,218
I won't use my palm.

178
00:22:46,386 --> 00:22:47,596
I'll use my fist.

179
00:22:57,230 --> 00:22:58,356
To be honest,

180
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:02,444
I was raging to go after Baek Sang-gil
more than anyone else was.

181
00:23:03,028 --> 00:23:06,781
But Prosecutor Go called to check in
on Jeong-hwa and said she'd handle it.

182
00:23:07,949 --> 00:23:11,495
Baek Sang-gil's been caught,
and she said she'd avenge Jeong-hwa.

183
00:23:11,578 --> 00:23:16,875
So this is where our role ends,
don't you think?

184
00:23:37,103 --> 00:23:38,313
You've endured so much.

185
00:23:40,941 --> 00:23:41,900
Let's go.

186
00:23:42,901 --> 00:23:45,612
Jeong-hwa is waiting for you.

187
00:23:48,782 --> 00:23:49,616
Let's go.

188
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:27,195
Tae-ha's here.

189
00:24:27,862 --> 00:24:29,781
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

190
00:24:44,629 --> 00:24:45,630
I'm sorry.

191
00:24:48,508 --> 00:24:49,551
Tae-ha.

192
00:25:11,114 --> 00:25:13,950
Those guys forgot

193
00:25:14,034 --> 00:25:16,286
that we're from Taffy Village.

194
00:25:17,412 --> 00:25:19,539
Let them start as many fires as they wish.

195
00:25:19,623 --> 00:25:25,045
Taffy doesn't crack the hotter it gets.
It just sticks together even more.

196
00:25:28,715 --> 00:25:33,219
We can just keep living
like we always have, okay?

197
00:26:04,584 --> 00:26:08,004
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

198
00:26:08,088 --> 00:26:09,464
Early this morning, my team…

199
00:26:10,382 --> 00:26:11,925
This tastes best when it's warm.

200
00:26:12,008 --> 00:26:13,718
-Goodness!
-Tasty, right?

201
00:26:13,802 --> 00:26:15,970
-It's so good.
-Yours is always the best.

202
00:26:16,471 --> 00:26:18,014
…both under emergency arrest.

203
00:26:18,973 --> 00:26:19,849
Eun-sae?

204
00:26:19,933 --> 00:26:20,850
What?

205
00:26:22,060 --> 00:26:24,229
-Holy smokes.
-Why bring up Eun-sae suddenly?

206
00:26:24,312 --> 00:26:28,483
…when the two exchanged cash
in return for Mayor Ju giving Mirae Eden…

207
00:26:28,566 --> 00:26:29,734
Why is she over there?

208
00:26:30,735 --> 00:26:32,320
Didn't she flee the country?

209
00:26:32,404 --> 00:26:34,155
-The Irang-dong project…
-Hold on.

210
00:26:34,239 --> 00:26:35,240
Then did she

211
00:26:36,658 --> 00:26:37,784
get her memory back?

212
00:26:39,494 --> 00:26:41,705
…increasing the gravity of the offense.

213
00:26:41,788 --> 00:26:43,790
I know that lady well.

214
00:26:44,374 --> 00:26:45,792
She's on TV.

215
00:26:47,460 --> 00:26:50,088
-Through call logs and internal documents…
-Hold up.

216
00:26:50,171 --> 00:26:52,716
Isn't this prosecutor Ms. Go Eun-sae?

217
00:26:54,259 --> 00:26:55,093
She got him.

218
00:26:55,176 --> 00:26:56,970
No way. This is insane.

219
00:26:57,470 --> 00:26:58,596
She actually got him.

220
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:02,350
…after which we plan to uncover
any further collusive ties

221
00:27:02,434 --> 00:27:04,894
and share our findings
as soon as possible.

222
00:27:04,978 --> 00:27:06,396
Attagirl, Go Eun-sae.

223
00:27:07,647 --> 00:27:11,109
Moreover, the people involved in this case
are being revealed one by one,

224
00:27:11,192 --> 00:27:15,238
and there are suspicions of internal leaks
within the prosecution.

225
00:27:15,321 --> 00:27:18,783
Thus, we plan to thoroughly investigate
all related scandals.

226
00:27:19,284 --> 00:27:20,118
Ji-won.

227
00:27:22,245 --> 00:27:24,372
Please cooperate with the investigation,
Aide Gwak.

228
00:27:31,463 --> 00:27:33,173
My investigation team and I

229
00:27:33,256 --> 00:27:36,676
vow to get to the bottom
of this chain of corruption

230
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:38,011
and shut it down.

231
00:28:02,786 --> 00:28:04,913
You made a name for yourself
as you wanted.

232
00:28:06,289 --> 00:28:07,624
I'm not there yet.

233
00:28:07,707 --> 00:28:10,376
If I'm to dig up everything that happened

234
00:28:10,460 --> 00:28:13,463
and make sure our chairman here
spends all his days in prison,

235
00:28:13,963 --> 00:28:15,423
this is just the beginning.

236
00:28:16,174 --> 00:28:17,675
Besides the bribery,

237
00:28:17,759 --> 00:28:20,595
I'd also been investigating other matters
in the background.

238
00:28:21,262 --> 00:28:24,682
The remains of several missing people
linked to the development project

239
00:28:24,766 --> 00:28:29,229
were found in the quarries and mountains
owned by Mirae Eden.

240
00:28:29,312 --> 00:28:33,149
So far, we've confirmed four murders
and the instigation of five more.

241
00:28:33,817 --> 00:28:36,861
But this is just the tip of the iceberg,

242
00:28:38,196 --> 00:28:39,197
is it not?

243
00:28:43,743 --> 00:28:48,540
I came to tell you not to waste your time
trying to reduce your sentence.

244
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:51,209
By the way,

245
00:28:51,292 --> 00:28:53,002
it turns out

246
00:28:53,503 --> 00:28:56,464
that some relationships
really are thicker than blood.

247
00:28:57,465 --> 00:29:00,635
It seems you had a scenario in mind
for Jang Tae-ha and Mr. Hong.

248
00:29:00,718 --> 00:29:04,305
It's a shame that even that
didn't go as you planned.

249
00:29:06,724 --> 00:29:08,268
See you around, Chairman.

250
00:29:28,413 --> 00:29:31,165
It's been two weeks
since Mirae Eden's Chairman Baek

251
00:29:31,249 --> 00:29:33,167
and Mayor Ju of Gangju City were arrested…

252
00:29:33,251 --> 00:29:35,837
Seeing her on the news from time to time
is nice and all

253
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,381
because we can see she's doing well.

254
00:29:38,882 --> 00:29:42,010
But isn't it a bit out of order
that she hasn't reached out once?

255
00:29:42,093 --> 00:29:44,971
Did she have to go as far
as to turn off her phone?

256
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:49,434
She's just gone back to her place.

257
00:29:50,184 --> 00:29:53,187
She didn't really belong
with the likes of us.

258
00:29:53,688 --> 00:29:57,025
Even if it was just a passing encounter,

259
00:29:57,650 --> 00:30:00,820
how can it end
without so much as a goodbye?

260
00:30:03,531 --> 00:30:04,532
How's Tae-ha doing?

261
00:30:05,116 --> 00:30:07,368
He's at the gym by himself,

262
00:30:07,452 --> 00:30:09,913
since Mr. Hong's by Jeong-hwa's bedside.

263
00:30:10,538 --> 00:30:13,458
It doesn't seem like Eun-sae has contacted
Tae-ha either, right?

264
00:30:13,541 --> 00:30:18,004
Seeing how he always goes back and forth
between the gym and his house…

265
00:30:18,504 --> 00:30:19,547
What's left to say?

266
00:30:20,173 --> 00:30:23,009
The prosecution will announce
the investigation's findings

267
00:30:23,092 --> 00:30:25,136
as soon as additional charges
are revealed.

268
00:30:47,367 --> 00:30:49,202
I only think about you all day long.

269
00:30:55,792 --> 00:31:00,171
The prosecution has conducted a search
and seizure of Mirae Eden's headquarters.

270
00:31:00,254 --> 00:31:03,174
Prosecutor Go Ji-won,
who is leading the investigation,

271
00:31:03,257 --> 00:31:06,094
has stated plans to thoroughly review
the evidence obtained

272
00:31:06,177 --> 00:31:07,845
to investigate any illegal activities.

273
00:31:07,929 --> 00:31:08,805
GO EUN-SAE

274
00:31:08,888 --> 00:31:11,432
Attention is focused on
uncovering those behind the case.

275
00:31:11,516 --> 00:31:13,518
My investigation team and I

276
00:31:13,601 --> 00:31:18,398
vow to get to the bottom of
this chain of corruption and shut it down.

277
00:31:50,263 --> 00:31:51,097
Okay.

278
00:31:54,809 --> 00:31:56,352
Hey, Prosecutor Go.

279
00:31:57,145 --> 00:31:59,313
I know it can't be helped
with such big fish,

280
00:31:59,397 --> 00:32:01,399
but you've been at it nonstop.
Are you okay?

281
00:32:02,608 --> 00:32:05,361
I had to get all the heavy lifting done
by today.

282
00:32:06,237 --> 00:32:07,739
I just finished all the work.

283
00:32:07,822 --> 00:32:09,115
Then can I

284
00:32:09,657 --> 00:32:11,743
go ahead with what I mentioned last time?

285
00:32:16,748 --> 00:32:17,582
What the heck?

286
00:32:23,296 --> 00:32:24,130
The heck is this?

287
00:32:36,309 --> 00:32:38,811
You can continue on your way. I've got it.

288
00:32:46,778 --> 00:32:47,612
Go Eun-sae.

289
00:32:51,574 --> 00:32:55,119
Looking at it now,
you're the one who's scared of toads.

290
00:32:55,203 --> 00:32:58,790
You came up with that weird story
because you were scared of them.

291
00:32:59,916 --> 00:33:00,750
What…

292
00:33:03,211 --> 00:33:04,587
What happened?

293
00:33:04,670 --> 00:33:06,130
Didn't you watch the news?

294
00:33:06,756 --> 00:33:09,300
I'm the busiest prosecutor in Korea
these days.

295
00:33:09,383 --> 00:33:11,511
I worked myself to the bone

296
00:33:11,594 --> 00:33:14,222
and finally managed to get a day off.

297
00:33:15,223 --> 00:33:16,432
To see my boyfriend.

298
00:33:20,812 --> 00:33:24,315
Why are you so surprised?
You are my boyfriend.

299
00:33:25,691 --> 00:33:27,360
When I said we should break up,

300
00:33:27,443 --> 00:33:30,947
I was lying so that I could move quietly
until I arrested them.

301
00:33:33,950 --> 00:33:34,784
Right.

302
00:33:35,952 --> 00:33:39,539
I really need to make the most
of my precious day off tomorrow.

303
00:33:40,289 --> 00:33:41,457
So

304
00:33:41,958 --> 00:33:44,210
will you do whatever I want from now on?

305
00:33:47,797 --> 00:33:49,966
-Sure.
-Yay!

306
00:33:55,763 --> 00:33:57,265
The ocean!

307
00:33:58,474 --> 00:34:01,978
I felt so restless, cooped up every day
in the prosecutor's office.

308
00:34:02,478 --> 00:34:05,022
It feels so refreshing!

309
00:34:06,566 --> 00:34:07,567
This is great.

310
00:34:13,406 --> 00:34:14,323
Careful. Don't fall.

311
00:34:14,407 --> 00:34:16,826
Don't worry. I'm super athlet--

312
00:34:19,829 --> 00:34:21,038
Are you okay?

313
00:34:28,337 --> 00:34:31,299
Do you know what I'm famous for
as a prosecutor these days?

314
00:34:35,553 --> 00:34:37,930
For chasing people until I catch them!

315
00:35:08,544 --> 00:35:10,755
-You wanted to come to the ocean?
-Yeah.

316
00:35:12,131 --> 00:35:15,384
My last memory of the ocean
was almost fleeing the country.

317
00:35:15,468 --> 00:35:17,470
The memory of both you and me
almost dying.

318
00:35:18,804 --> 00:35:21,182
We need to overwrite it
with good memories.

319
00:35:29,815 --> 00:35:33,361
Why did you go so far to save me?

320
00:35:35,488 --> 00:35:37,240
When you got me to flee the country,

321
00:35:37,323 --> 00:35:39,825
when you disobeyed orders and hid me away,

322
00:35:40,618 --> 00:35:43,496
those were all things
that put you in serious danger.

323
00:35:44,997 --> 00:35:49,502
Even though we had met before,
it happened only twice in our lives.

324
00:35:51,462 --> 00:35:54,632
Why did you go so far
as to risk your life to save me?

325
00:36:03,891 --> 00:36:05,142
You're the only one.

326
00:36:07,687 --> 00:36:10,731
You're the only person I've ever liked.

327
00:36:15,778 --> 00:36:18,614
That night I spent with you in Japan…

328
00:36:20,366 --> 00:36:23,661
was the first time I ever wished
time would go by slower.

329
00:36:26,747 --> 00:36:28,958
Each second felt so precious.

330
00:36:30,001 --> 00:36:30,835
I was that happy.

331
00:36:37,550 --> 00:36:39,260
How could I not have been?

332
00:36:40,511 --> 00:36:41,637
You were my first love.

333
00:36:44,849 --> 00:36:45,975
First love?

334
00:36:46,684 --> 00:36:49,103
That one. Is that yours?

335
00:36:49,186 --> 00:36:51,564
Yeah, it's a medal I got back
thanks to my first love.

336
00:36:52,773 --> 00:36:54,608
But I like this one the most.

337
00:36:55,526 --> 00:36:57,111
I met my first love here.

338
00:36:57,737 --> 00:36:58,863
Wait, so you…

339
00:36:58,946 --> 00:37:01,449
You've liked me
ever since that boxing match years ago?

340
00:37:07,038 --> 00:37:08,998
2010 NATIONAL JUNIOR BOXING TEAM SELECTION

341
00:37:17,548 --> 00:37:20,051
Why does he keep hitting his eye?

342
00:37:26,015 --> 00:37:26,974
What's up with him?

343
00:37:28,934 --> 00:37:30,561
-All done.
-Okay.

344
00:37:30,644 --> 00:37:31,979
Red fighter.

345
00:37:32,063 --> 00:37:33,272
Blue.

346
00:37:41,447 --> 00:37:42,698
Tae-ha, open your eyes.

347
00:38:12,645 --> 00:38:14,146
They cheated in this match.

348
00:38:15,689 --> 00:38:18,401
Kid, you can't just
recklessly barge in here.

349
00:38:19,276 --> 00:38:21,862
I'm not being reckless.
I came here prudently.

350
00:38:27,952 --> 00:38:29,036
Damn it.

351
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:31,455
I wonder if this is just disinfectant.

352
00:38:34,041 --> 00:38:35,292
Look here, kid!

353
00:38:37,294 --> 00:38:39,338
I saw something
while I was taking selfies.

354
00:39:15,332 --> 00:39:16,876
I guess we should give him a cut.

355
00:39:16,959 --> 00:39:19,211
He'll get a cut soon enough.

356
00:39:19,920 --> 00:39:20,754
Just trust me.

357
00:39:26,969 --> 00:39:28,095
You little…

358
00:39:28,179 --> 00:39:29,805
Sir, what are you doing?

359
00:39:29,889 --> 00:39:31,140
Let go of me and talk.

360
00:39:31,223 --> 00:39:33,142
Coach, talk it out. Come on.

361
00:39:42,610 --> 00:39:44,612
Okay, I'll take the picture now.

362
00:39:44,695 --> 00:39:46,906
One, two, three.

363
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:51,285
You know me, Grandma. Of course I won.

364
00:39:52,286 --> 00:39:54,872
I'll stop by the village
with my gold medal this weekend.

365
00:39:55,664 --> 00:39:56,499
Okay.

366
00:39:59,919 --> 00:40:00,794
Hey.

367
00:40:01,712 --> 00:40:02,922
About earlier…

368
00:40:03,839 --> 00:40:04,882
Thank you.

369
00:40:06,634 --> 00:40:08,886
You don't have to be so formal.
I'm a first-year.

370
00:40:10,346 --> 00:40:12,848
Did you come to cheer for your friend?

371
00:40:13,432 --> 00:40:14,892
An orphanage friend had a match.

372
00:40:16,101 --> 00:40:18,479
Wasn't I sort of awesome earlier?

373
00:40:19,647 --> 00:40:21,232
I stepped in with the evidence

374
00:40:21,315 --> 00:40:23,776
and changed the color of your medal
with my own hands.

375
00:40:23,859 --> 00:40:24,735
Wow.

376
00:40:24,818 --> 00:40:27,363
Even I have to admit
it was seriously badass.

377
00:40:28,364 --> 00:40:32,409
Like a righteous prosecutor
who's committed to rooting out corruption.

378
00:40:32,493 --> 00:40:34,078
Maybe that's what I'll become.

379
00:40:34,161 --> 00:40:35,579
Do you get good grades?

380
00:40:35,663 --> 00:40:38,749
If they gave out medals for grades,
I'd have a gold medal too.

381
00:40:40,042 --> 00:40:41,544
Remember me when you make it.

382
00:40:42,253 --> 00:40:45,130
Without me,
you would have missed out on a medal.

383
00:40:45,714 --> 00:40:49,677
Okay. When I win Olympic gold,
I'll shout you out in my interview.

384
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:52,012
All right, I'll be watching.

385
00:40:53,389 --> 00:40:56,475
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

386
00:41:06,151 --> 00:41:07,152
Tae-ha!

387
00:41:07,945 --> 00:41:09,572
What are you doing over there?

388
00:41:09,655 --> 00:41:12,074
I'll be right there.

389
00:41:17,830 --> 00:41:18,747
Your name…

390
00:41:34,388 --> 00:41:36,265
What was his name again?

391
00:41:37,683 --> 00:41:39,310
I want to remember it.

392
00:41:45,941 --> 00:41:47,776
So you fell for me back then.

393
00:41:50,362 --> 00:41:54,033
Then why didn't you give me
your number in Japan?

394
00:41:54,116 --> 00:41:55,701
I was your first love, after all.

395
00:41:59,079 --> 00:42:02,207
You'd grown up well,
just like how you were back then.

396
00:42:03,417 --> 00:42:05,210
But instead of winning an Olympic gold…

397
00:42:07,379 --> 00:42:08,422
I became a gangster.

398
00:42:19,433 --> 00:42:21,560
I didn't exactly become
a righteous prosecutor.

399
00:42:22,811 --> 00:42:26,273
Once I actually became a prosecutor,
I grew hungry for success.

400
00:42:27,441 --> 00:42:30,444
Coming from nothing,
I was obsessed with proving myself.

401
00:42:31,403 --> 00:42:34,281
But doing all that
only left me feeling empty,

402
00:42:34,365 --> 00:42:37,743
so I splurged on expensive bags
and supercars.

403
00:42:38,243 --> 00:42:40,913
The reason I was so unimpressed
by everything

404
00:42:40,996 --> 00:42:42,956
when I first came to Taffy Village

405
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:46,210
must have been because I had become
such a materialistic person.

406
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:52,257
I guess it's hard to become the cool adult
you dreamed of being as a kid.

407
00:43:01,600 --> 00:43:06,563
It turns out that some relationships
really are thicker than blood.

408
00:43:10,984 --> 00:43:12,027
You little punk.

409
00:43:12,111 --> 00:43:15,531
Where did you hide it?
Hand it over, you bastard!

410
00:43:15,614 --> 00:43:17,408
Your father wants to gamble a little.

411
00:43:17,491 --> 00:43:19,993
So where's the money
you took from your friends, punk?

412
00:43:20,077 --> 00:43:22,413
How many times must I tell you?
I don't have any!

413
00:43:22,496 --> 00:43:23,497
You don't?

414
00:43:23,580 --> 00:43:25,749
You bastard.
Then you should get beaten up.

415
00:43:25,833 --> 00:43:27,042
You should get beaten--

416
00:43:27,668 --> 00:43:29,920
Let go, you bastard! Let go!

417
00:43:30,003 --> 00:43:33,507
You son of a bitch!
How dare you grab my hand!

418
00:43:41,014 --> 00:43:43,225
FUNERAL HOME

419
00:43:46,854 --> 00:43:49,064
THE LATE BAEK HAK-SU

420
00:43:53,986 --> 00:43:55,654
You did something pointless.

421
00:43:55,738 --> 00:43:57,114
Turn the car around.

422
00:43:59,575 --> 00:44:03,495
A scum of a father
who beat up his kid every day

423
00:44:03,579 --> 00:44:05,914
so his bruises could never fade…

424
00:44:07,958 --> 00:44:09,334
doesn't deserve a send-off.

425
00:44:10,502 --> 00:44:12,713
I hope you'll prove it, sir.

426
00:44:13,881 --> 00:44:15,466
That you're different from him.

427
00:44:18,469 --> 00:44:19,928
I'll get us some drinks.

428
00:44:28,061 --> 00:44:29,188
Jang Tae-ha.

429
00:44:29,271 --> 00:44:31,482
You've never once disappointed me.

430
00:44:31,565 --> 00:44:34,693
I don't know about the others,
but I trust you.

431
00:44:50,793 --> 00:44:53,170
Understood. I'll get things ready.

432
00:44:59,510 --> 00:45:00,761
Cheers!

433
00:45:07,726 --> 00:45:08,852
This is it!

434
00:45:08,936 --> 00:45:11,730
I couldn't drink a single drop
because of work.

435
00:45:11,814 --> 00:45:15,609
It must have been… a month
since I last drank soju in Taffy Village.

436
00:45:16,485 --> 00:45:18,111
-With the ladies?
-Yes.

437
00:45:18,695 --> 00:45:20,614
I drank with the ladies.

438
00:45:22,115 --> 00:45:26,411
Also at a pub with Dr. An Gi-jun
when he ended up carrying me home

439
00:45:26,495 --> 00:45:28,247
because I was upset thanks to someone.

440
00:45:34,503 --> 00:45:38,048
You know, I thought Dr. An Gi-jun
was a weirdo at first,

441
00:45:38,131 --> 00:45:41,343
but the more I get to know him,
he's pretty cute.

442
00:45:42,052 --> 00:45:45,389
Born to be cute, if you will.
You just can't hate him, whatever he does.

443
00:45:51,478 --> 00:45:53,313
I'd say cats are what you call cute.

444
00:46:07,870 --> 00:46:09,246
Why is this pepper so spicy?

445
00:46:11,665 --> 00:46:14,251
What's so cute about a 34-year-old man?

446
00:46:14,835 --> 00:46:16,336
You're not jealous, are you?

447
00:46:16,879 --> 00:46:18,422
-I'm not.
-But you are.

448
00:46:19,798 --> 00:46:21,216
You are jealous right now!

449
00:46:22,551 --> 00:46:25,596
I guess a 34-year-old man can be cute.

450
00:46:27,222 --> 00:46:30,017
Dr. An Gi-jun likes someone.

451
00:46:30,100 --> 00:46:32,895
A woman with eyes that point to 8:20.

452
00:46:32,978 --> 00:46:34,313
Doors opening.

453
00:46:48,577 --> 00:46:51,622
Let's break up now.

454
00:46:52,748 --> 00:46:53,582
Whatever.

455
00:46:53,665 --> 00:46:56,084
I'm just here to pick up my stuff.

456
00:46:58,503 --> 00:47:00,088
Doors opening.

457
00:47:16,647 --> 00:47:18,941
I suddenly remembered
that I left some stuff here.

458
00:47:19,524 --> 00:47:20,442
Right.

459
00:47:29,284 --> 00:47:32,037
You're going home like that?

460
00:47:32,955 --> 00:47:34,039
Yeah, I'll take a taxi.

461
00:47:34,122 --> 00:47:36,875
It's rush hour, so you won't catch one.
Just ride with me.

462
00:48:11,451 --> 00:48:13,620
Hyeon-seong's favorite random game!

463
00:48:13,704 --> 00:48:14,538
2 YEARS AGO

464
00:48:15,914 --> 00:48:18,041
Tap your glass.

465
00:48:22,004 --> 00:48:22,879
It's Su-ji!

466
00:48:24,589 --> 00:48:26,675
-Your timing was off.
-Su-ji, drink!

467
00:48:29,052 --> 00:48:32,055
Su-ji's favorite random game!

468
00:48:33,557 --> 00:48:34,391
Double-oh…

469
00:48:34,474 --> 00:48:35,392
Seven!

470
00:48:36,018 --> 00:48:37,144
-Bang!
-Ugh!

471
00:48:37,227 --> 00:48:38,687
Double-oh seven…

472
00:48:38,770 --> 00:48:40,272
Bang! Ugh!

473
00:48:41,231 --> 00:48:42,733
You can't just scare her…

474
00:48:42,816 --> 00:48:44,776
Su-ji, you're awful at games.

475
00:48:45,277 --> 00:48:47,029
I'll be her black knight.

476
00:48:48,155 --> 00:48:50,949
Hey, the black knight? Out of nowhere?

477
00:48:51,033 --> 00:48:52,242
What a party pooper.

478
00:48:52,325 --> 00:48:54,036
Hey, don't tell me…

479
00:48:54,119 --> 00:48:56,079
-What is it?
-Class pres, what's up?

480
00:48:56,663 --> 00:48:58,623
-Is something going on?
-Are you two…

481
00:48:58,707 --> 00:49:00,000
Caring for your employee?

482
00:49:00,083 --> 00:49:02,085
-What? No, I…
-That's what it is.

483
00:49:02,169 --> 00:49:03,086
Yeah, I mean…

484
00:49:03,170 --> 00:49:05,130
Of course. She's my employee, so…

485
00:49:05,714 --> 00:49:08,508
From now on, I'll drink for Min Su-ji.
Since I'm her boss.

486
00:49:08,592 --> 00:49:10,260
-Nice, Dr. An!
-Keep going.

487
00:49:10,343 --> 00:49:11,470
Okay, then let's…

488
00:49:12,262 --> 00:49:14,264
-Hey.
-Let's take things up a notch.

489
00:49:14,347 --> 00:49:15,682
-He must be nuts.
-Okay.

490
00:49:15,766 --> 00:49:16,641
Read-the-room game…

491
00:49:16,725 --> 00:49:18,143
-What?
-Read-the-room game.

492
00:49:18,226 --> 00:49:19,102
One.

493
00:49:19,186 --> 00:49:20,771
-Two.
-Three.

494
00:49:20,854 --> 00:49:21,855
-Four!
-Four!

495
00:49:22,898 --> 00:49:23,982
Come on!

496
00:49:24,066 --> 00:49:25,942
All right, Gi-jun, drink first.

497
00:49:26,026 --> 00:49:27,110
Just drink together.

498
00:49:27,194 --> 00:49:28,528
Hey, I…

499
00:49:33,492 --> 00:49:35,452
-I'll drink that for you.
-You already…

500
00:49:35,535 --> 00:49:37,120
I'm fine. Really.

501
00:49:37,746 --> 00:49:39,414
I usually drink fast.

502
00:49:45,962 --> 00:49:47,714
Gi-jun, get a hold of yourself.

503
00:49:49,925 --> 00:49:51,259
Su-ji's watching.

504
00:49:51,343 --> 00:49:52,844
You can't look weak.

505
00:49:53,512 --> 00:49:54,346
Be cool.

506
00:49:54,930 --> 00:49:55,972
Act cool.

507
00:50:02,062 --> 00:50:02,896
Let's try it.

508
00:50:02,979 --> 00:50:05,440
Can I talk to you without formalities
outside of work?

509
00:50:05,941 --> 00:50:06,775
We're classmates.

510
00:50:07,776 --> 00:50:08,610
Is that too much?

511
00:50:08,693 --> 00:50:11,154
I'll talk casually outside of work.
We're classmates.

512
00:50:11,238 --> 00:50:12,239
What a loser.

513
00:50:12,322 --> 00:50:13,490
Outside the… The clinic…

514
00:50:13,573 --> 00:50:15,992
We're not at work, so I'll be informal.
Can I?

515
00:50:16,076 --> 00:50:17,035
Let's be informal.

516
00:50:17,619 --> 00:50:18,787
Since we're classmates.

517
00:50:19,996 --> 00:50:21,123
Okay, like that.

518
00:50:24,876 --> 00:50:27,003
Can I talk casually outside of work?
Since we…

519
00:50:27,587 --> 00:50:30,882
We can talk casually
outside the clinic, right?

520
00:50:30,966 --> 00:50:32,759
Classmates… Damn, what's with my hair?

521
00:50:34,010 --> 00:50:35,303
Should I touch it up again?

522
00:50:36,513 --> 00:50:38,348
-I should touch it up a little.
-Hey.

523
00:50:38,431 --> 00:50:39,349
Huh?

524
00:50:42,978 --> 00:50:45,313
Can I touch you up outside of work?
As classmates?

525
00:50:45,397 --> 00:50:46,898
-What?
-What?

526
00:50:48,108 --> 00:50:50,777
No, wait. That's not it. Really.

527
00:50:50,861 --> 00:50:52,529
I didn't mean that.

528
00:50:52,612 --> 00:50:54,781
I mean, how could I dare to…

529
00:50:54,865 --> 00:50:57,617
My hair. I was talking about my hair.

530
00:51:02,247 --> 00:51:04,583
Let's talk casually outside of work.
As classmates.

531
00:51:04,666 --> 00:51:05,667
What?

532
00:51:06,418 --> 00:51:07,335
Sure.

533
00:51:07,919 --> 00:51:09,296
Is your stomach okay?

534
00:51:09,796 --> 00:51:11,506
Why did you take my drinks for me?

535
00:51:11,590 --> 00:51:13,842
In case you were tired.
You shouldn't get sick.

536
00:51:13,925 --> 00:51:15,385
I can drink up to three bottles.

537
00:51:15,969 --> 00:51:17,971
-What?
-You said your limit is two shots.

538
00:51:18,763 --> 00:51:21,474
No, it's not. I can hold my liquor.

539
00:51:28,732 --> 00:51:29,858
Want some hangover soup?

540
00:51:32,110 --> 00:51:34,112
-What?
-Your stomach's upset right now.

541
00:51:37,282 --> 00:51:38,116
Don't have time?

542
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:40,702
I do. I totally do, do.

543
00:51:40,785 --> 00:51:42,495
Not like doo-doo, I mean…

544
00:51:44,080 --> 00:51:47,292
I should get rid of my hangover.
I could even go for a hangover drink.

545
00:51:56,885 --> 00:51:57,719
Are you okay?

546
00:52:08,480 --> 00:52:10,065
I just thought of something funny.

547
00:52:22,869 --> 00:52:23,703
Thank you.

548
00:52:25,622 --> 00:52:27,457
Is there anything else you wanted to do?

549
00:52:28,208 --> 00:52:30,210
-Yes.
-What is it?

550
00:52:30,710 --> 00:52:31,878
Should we…

551
00:52:36,800 --> 00:52:38,051
get some rest?

552
00:52:38,760 --> 00:52:39,844
What?

553
00:52:39,928 --> 00:52:42,347
There's something I really want to do.

554
00:52:44,432 --> 00:52:45,558
Over there?

555
00:52:46,393 --> 00:52:47,519
What exactly?

556
00:52:48,061 --> 00:52:49,521
Let's get some rest.

557
00:52:49,604 --> 00:52:53,358
I'm not trying to pull anything.
There's something I really want to do.

558
00:52:53,441 --> 00:52:54,567
Okay?

559
00:52:56,444 --> 00:52:58,280
But what could we do over there?

560
00:53:16,506 --> 00:53:18,883
So this is what you meant by "rest."

561
00:53:22,971 --> 00:53:23,805
I see.

562
00:53:25,724 --> 00:53:26,850
Right.

563
00:53:28,476 --> 00:53:32,188
Is this that thing that's trending lately?
Fire watching?

564
00:53:35,400 --> 00:53:36,776
It's time.

565
00:53:37,360 --> 00:53:38,695
Happy birthday.

566
00:53:40,363 --> 00:53:41,197
What?

567
00:53:42,449 --> 00:53:43,616
It's your birthday today.

568
00:53:45,702 --> 00:53:47,412
See? I wasn't trying anything funny.

569
00:53:48,580 --> 00:53:50,332
This is why I asked to come here.

570
00:53:53,084 --> 00:53:55,295
-To wish me a happy birthday?
-Yeah.

571
00:53:56,755 --> 00:53:58,840
It wasn't just you.

572
00:53:59,341 --> 00:54:01,634
I also really enjoyed that night.

573
00:54:05,388 --> 00:54:07,807
The pleasant sea breeze.

574
00:54:08,892 --> 00:54:10,894
The crackling of the campfire.

575
00:54:23,198 --> 00:54:25,325
The beautiful sunrise.

576
00:54:26,576 --> 00:54:27,452
And…

577
00:54:35,043 --> 00:54:37,087
Happy birthday.

578
00:54:40,423 --> 00:54:43,385
A "happy birthday"
from a guy I found attractive.

579
00:54:44,177 --> 00:54:48,640
It was the best birthday of my life,
so I wanted to do the same for you.

580
00:54:56,606 --> 00:55:00,026
Do you know how hard I worked
to get a day off?

581
00:55:01,069 --> 00:55:03,613
I knew that if I contacted you
or anyone in the village,

582
00:55:03,696 --> 00:55:05,323
I'd want to come right away.

583
00:55:05,407 --> 00:55:06,783
So I even kept my phone off.

584
00:55:06,866 --> 00:55:09,911
I worked my butt off for days and nights

585
00:55:09,994 --> 00:55:12,205
to finish my work and come here.

586
00:55:14,999 --> 00:55:18,294
Why did you go through all that trouble
just for my birthday?

587
00:55:24,259 --> 00:55:25,552
I love you.

588
00:55:31,724 --> 00:55:32,725
Why are you surprised?

589
00:55:36,020 --> 00:55:40,692
How could I not love the fool
who put his life on the line

590
00:55:41,651 --> 00:55:44,112
just to save me?

591
00:55:47,282 --> 00:55:51,202
Someday, when time has passed
and your memory has returned…

592
00:55:51,286 --> 00:55:53,121
My memory has returned…

593
00:55:53,204 --> 00:55:55,999
…and even if the day comes
when you don't like me anymore…

594
00:55:56,082 --> 00:55:58,042
…but I still like Jang Tae-ha.

595
00:55:58,877 --> 00:56:00,336
I hope our time together

596
00:56:00,420 --> 00:56:03,047
won't be a painful memory for you.

597
00:56:03,923 --> 00:56:06,843
And the time I spent
as Jang Tae-ha's girlfriend

598
00:56:07,343 --> 00:56:09,095
was the happiest time

599
00:56:09,804 --> 00:56:10,930
of my life.

600
00:56:14,851 --> 00:56:16,561
Thank you so much

601
00:56:17,729 --> 00:56:19,689
for coming into this world

602
00:56:20,398 --> 00:56:21,941
and for coming into my life.

603
00:56:24,903 --> 00:56:26,654
I really, truly…

604
00:56:28,490 --> 00:56:29,741
love you.

605
00:57:51,155 --> 00:57:52,824
OUR STICKY LOVE

606
00:58:39,454 --> 00:58:43,416
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

